import{_ as a,o as t,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.D66Xq0Kv.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Mail","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"guide/mail.md","filePath":"guide/mail.md"}'),s={name:"guide/mail.md"};function i(r,e,d,l,c,m){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="mail" tabindex="-1">Mail <a class="header-anchor" href="#mail" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Mail&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The <strong>Email</strong> page brings Hostinger Email mailboxes into a workspace: folders, server-side search, message reading, attachments, read and starred flags, moving messages, and composing or replying. Messages stay at Hostinger. Orbit does not keep a local copy of your inbox.</p><h2 id="connect-a-mailbox" tabindex="-1">Connect a mailbox <a class="header-anchor" href="#connect-a-mailbox" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Connect a mailbox {#connect-a-mailbox}&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>In Hostinger, select your email domain and open <strong>Agentic Mail → API access</strong>. See the <a href="https://docs.hostinger.com/emails/mail-api" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Hostinger Mail API guide</a> for the provider&#39;s setup instructions.</li><li>Create a Mail API token restricted to the mailboxes you want to share. Grant the permissions needed to read, send, and organize messages.</li><li>In Orbit, open <strong>Email → Connect Hostinger Mail</strong> and enter the token.</li></ol><p>This is a <strong>Hostinger Mail API</strong> token. The Hostinger token used for DNS and VPS cannot authenticate the Mail API. Titan mailboxes are not supported by this integration.</p><p>Orbit validates the token before saving it encrypted in the secret store. Each workspace has its own connection. All mailboxes accessible to that token become available to that workspace, so restrict the token at Hostinger before connecting it. Reconnecting replaces the token; disconnecting removes it from Orbit without deleting mail or folders at Hostinger.</p><h2 id="who-can-use-it" tabindex="-1">Who can use it <a class="header-anchor" href="#who-can-use-it" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Who can use it {#who-can-use-it}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>On the <strong>Email</strong> page, wide screens show the message list alongside the open message. On smaller screens, opening a message brings up a reading panel. Choose <strong>Reply</strong> to write from the selected mailbox, or <strong>Archive</strong> to move the message to its archive folder. An inline reply stays with its original workspace, mailbox and message while you switch views on the Email page. Leaving the page or reloading it clears these in-memory drafts.</p><p>Workspace viewers can read and download attachments. Developers can also send, mark messages, and move them. Workspace admins can connect and disconnect. Orbit administrators can manage every workspace. Mailbox access follows workspace membership; individual per-mailbox assignments inside a workspace are not provided.</p><h2 id="reading-and-writing" tabindex="-1">Reading and writing <a class="header-anchor" href="#reading-and-writing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Reading and writing {#reading-and-writing}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Search runs on Hostinger across the selected folder, including headers and body. Results are paginated. Refresh reloads messages and folder counts. Opening a message leaves its read state unchanged; use <strong>Mark as read</strong> to update it. <strong>Archive</strong> and <strong>Move to trash</strong> move messages to the provider&#39;s corresponding folders; the interface does not permanently delete messages.</p><p>The Email page shows plain text and attachment names. In <strong>Manage email</strong>, HTML messages open inside a sanitized, sandboxed document, and attachments download through Orbit after it checks workspace and mailbox access. Both readers block remote images.</p><p>Compose supports To, Cc, Bcc, a subject, and plain-text body. Replies carry the original folder and message UID so Hostinger can preserve the thread. Hostinger saves sent messages in Sent. Outgoing attachments and persistent drafts are not yet supported. When composing in <strong>Manage email</strong>, the draft stays in the open composer, with a warning before discarding or leaving the page.</p><p>Orbit confirms sending only after Hostinger accepts it. It never automatically retries a send. If a network failure makes the result uncertain, check Sent in Hostinger before trying again; the composer keeps your draft.</p><h2 id="motion" tabindex="-1">Motion <a class="header-anchor" href="#motion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Motion {#motion}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The mail interface uses the official <code>@rafaelaugusto/jolt/web</code> runtime for message entrances, reader transitions, and the accepted-send confirmation. It follows the operating system&#39;s reduced-motion preference and disposes its runtime when the view closes.</p><h2 id="try-the-demo" tabindex="-1">Try the demo <a class="header-anchor" href="#try-the-demo" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Try the demo {#try-the-demo}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The demo console has <strong>Explore a demo inbox</strong> with eight fictional messages, including formatted newsletters and a downloadable sample attachment. Opening <code>/#/mail?demo=1</code> in the demo console connects the sample inbox and opens a message automatically. Existing changes to a demo inbox are preserved on reload.</p><p>Live builds connect to Hostinger and do not contain demo mail. The preview parameter has no effect in a live build. Connecting an actual mailbox requires its Mail API token; testing the demo does not verify a real account&#39;s permissions or delivery.</p>',19)])])}const p=a(s,[["render",i]]);export{h as __pageData,p as default};
